<title>USA: U.S. business loans rose $1.59 bln in Sept 25 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. business loans rose $1.59 bln in Sept 25 wk.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans on the books of U.S. commercial banks, excluding acceptances, rose $1.59 billion to $365.87 billion in the week ended Sept 25, the Federal Reserve said Friday.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $1.64 billion to $367.63 billion, the Fed said.</p>
</text>
